# Branch → local → prod

PaeScape (`Paepay/tsps`) uses a staged integration path. Do not treat `prod` as the
default merge target.

1. **Feature branches.** Do work on a focused branch off the current integration tip
   (usually `origin/local`, or `origin/prod` only if `local` does not exist yet).
2. **Review, then land on `local`.** After review, merge and push to the `local`
   branch. That is where the user plays and verifies changes. Prefer a PR into
   `local`, or merge locally and `git push origin local`, when asked to merge/push
   without naming `prod`.
3. **User tests on `local`.** Do not assume gameplay sign-off from agent checks alone.
   The user runs their own server/client against `local`.
4. **Promote to `prod` only when asked.** Merge/push/deploy to `prod` only after the
   user says the `local` batch is good to go (or explicitly asks to ship/deploy to
   prod). Never default “merge and push” to `prod`.

When the user says only “merge and push”, target **`local`**. When they say ship,
deploy, or promote to prod, target **`prod`**.
